    "numeric_role_inventory": {
      "464:1..400": "Actual generated-row reexports are references, not generated-body coverage. Narrow first-party views retain raw numeric roles: Character IDu64, XP/levelu32, ageu16, notification usize and life/temporary/chat booleans; Settlement raw geographic f64, population leveli32/estimateu32 and optional source nodeu64; CaseBattle/Party gateway bucketu8 and actor/leader IDs; Party fatigue percentu8, daily/start minutesu16, elapsed/remainingu64, three f32 target ranks and explicit optional camp endpoint/typed anchorMinute; action requestu64 ID/requester; route weather versions/basis pointsu16, metres/minutesu64 and native generated point/span records; equipment inventory/character/parent IDs u64 and capacity/orderu16; recruitment ID/quantity/combat power; mission requester/required kill count. CatalogItemView retains massf32, volumeu32, raw reach/block/coverage/precision/resistance/padding/flexibility/ROM/inertia/balance/durability sensitivities, melee/ranged/repairable modes, optional base-valueu32, nutritionf32, water/container/alcohol volumesu32, alcohol basis points/effectivenessu16, qualityu8 and physical capability booleans. These are first-party retained view fields before actual templates/helpers, not a blanket native-wire exemption. Existing typed enums, RoleRequirements, WeaponSkillDistribution and geographic/economy profiles are carried where present. Purpose-specific existing owners and exact producer/consumer contracts must determine repair; do not force all booleans or optional zeros into invalid modes.",
      "464:401..819": "Actual From/TryFrom projections destructure generated native rows. CharacterView intentionally supplies current_case_site=None and notification/chat defaults pending explicit enrichment; no lost-field defect without the actual enrichment callers. Settlement maps native coord_x/y unchanged and converts nested languages/industry/economy through sats_to_serde, so native coordinate admission remains a dependency. CaseBattle and Party convert CaseSiteId through checked owner; Party anchor wraps all-u64 StrategicMinute, while other raw numeric roles are copied. PartyJourneyRoute wraps weather intervalMinute and copies raw weather/distance/duration/points/spans. Equipped item name and recruitment combat power intentionally start empty/zero for enrichment. Pending MissionServer uses typed status with empty transport fields; ready server sets actual address/identity. Optional/phase representation policy is separate from numeric validation. No ordinary missing-field or unsupported compatibility claim inferred from these staged views.",
      "464:820..1123": "Catalog projection carries unitmass, volumes, combat and condition attributes unchanged; exhaustive typed equipment location/channel/body-part conversion preserves enum roles. Raw capacity/order remain distinct semantic ordinals. Default catalog item is a simple empty placeholder with zero fields and no capabilities: actual consumers must determine admission before it can be called invalid runtime equipment. ItemConditionExt reads five f32 tiers; total sums and clamps0..1, repairable/residual sum take/skip skill.min5. Actual native condition admission is needed before overflow/negative/NaN claims; zero skill and unrepairable bins may be valid. Religion/oral/written/bestiary extension traits delegate to canonical core hours conversion and effective methods, connecting015 language/hour contract without another-lens transfer.",
      "464:1124..1921": "Closed native-to-core enum matches cover body/route/personality/equipment/status/religious shapes and preserve typed unavailable reason plus boolean travel option and raw wait minutes. Native learning-hour/weapon-weight/role-requirement fields are copied into first-party core records without new bounds here; the actual owning types and mutators still govern admission. All-zero language constructors represent no learned hours, valid absence. sats_to_serde serializes native SerdeWrapper then recursively normalizes sum-shaped JSON before checked core Deserialize. Singleton object+empty array becomes a unit tag; whether a legitimate singleton empty-list record reaches this route requires actual native schema/Serde proof. Normalization itself is not labeled a compatibility defect. one-field/one-variant expects follow exact len==1 immutable ownership, so ordinary empty iteration is disproved; production rule/representation case remains. String enum names and payload conversion policy remain distinct from numeric owner gaps.",
      "464:1922..2523": "All tests were read as source only, never executed. Fixtures include typed generated enum/profile values, numeric IDs7/52/53 and gateway buckets1..6; geographic Lubeck10.6866/53.8655, population22000, valid land-use10000, stone100%, language10000/incidence125, economy version10; travel edge1250m/slope1.25/certainty90 and typed endpoint progress0/1000. Catalog fixture unitmass1.25/volume900, order2/3/capacity2/order4, combat values.4..1.3, price25, quality3 and six durability fields.11..66. Tests assert intentional base-view defaults, explicit gateway/enrichment fields, typed case-site conversion, route minutes500, raw targets2/3/4, strict nested unknown-field rejection and investigation wait45 independent of prose. These do not prove successful runtime decoding or current schema coherence. Invalid or obsolete fixture behavior is not a compatibility requirement.",
      "465:original2053..2054/2090..2140 plus extensions2055..2089/2141..2208": "Now personally assessed exact connected union2053..2208, not full3812 and no SkillTooltip coverage. ActivityEffectRates privately stores raw f32 gold/reputation/morale/fatigue per-hour values, prayer multiplier/limit/scale minutes and a prayer-mode bool. LeisurePreview retains raw current fatigue/display plus core LeisureOutcome. Native ScheduleAllocation fields are mapped to DailySchedule; leisure outcome uses canonical settlement function then subtracts labor contribution and converts display points. effective_preview_schedule calls canonical crate::schedule::effective with typed location/seed, but uses expect on supposedly write-validated saved schedule; actual writer/admission/current bodies remain a dependency. preview_allocated_minutes delegates to canonical strategic time helper. Linear/prayer/meditation/carousing constructors have legitimate alternate modes; meditation quarter multiplier is authored local policy requiring exact core authority comparison before duplication claim. values converts minutes/60, computes exponential prayer effect or linear hourly effect, rounds only gold, and returns an unlabeled[f32;4] for currency/reputation/morale/fatigue. These application-specific rates and result roles need canonical owners/named records; actual cell/producer callers and canonical activity function are unread. Default zero fields are not by themselves an ordinary division error because prayer mode defaultsfalse.",
      "466:1..80": "Exact pinned WebSocket native backend. Wasm accepts String target at web_sys::WebSocket::new and classifies JS/CreateSocket error; native request conversion and TLS setup classify CreateTarget/Connect and split sessions. config.nagle inversion is native socket boolean, local/peer addresses are native. oneshot send failure maps FrontendClosed; backend returns Never-or-disconnect. Unexpected TLS stream panic is third-party configuration conditional, not a demonstrated first-party ordinary failure or a repair instruction. No raw application numeric role or SDK-wide proof.",
      "467:73..170": "Exact native WebSocketClient::connect boundary: Into<String> for wasm, IntoClientRequest for native, closure queues EntityCommand, oneshot channels and runtime task carry typed errors. Raw URI port1234 is documentation only; native config fields/types outside range are unread. Native mutable ECS/session lifecycle is shown only in exact functions; no global disconnect/despawn or reconnect SDK guarantee. No obsolete error prose/downcasts preservation.",
