      "469:389..440": "Exact native LinearVelocity component wraps Vector, derives native reflection/serialization/Deref and provides ZERO; acceleration2 and max speed100 are documentation examples only. This is the actual external physics velocity boundary for earlier385/399/412. It does not prove finite invariant, native engine integration, mass behavior or complete MaxLinearSpeed definition:440 is only an attribute before that body.",
      "470:175..290": "Exact Replicon native default serialization uses postcard, default deserialization creates a complete C then calls C::map_entities, and in-place helper assigns only after successful deserialize. Raw Vec<u8>/Bytes are native codec formats. consume_as_deserialize temporarily sets ctx.ignore_mapping=true and clears after successful call; an error returns before clearing, but actual context lifetime/reuse/abort policy is unread, so no ordinary poisoned-context failure is declared. serialize_as/deserialize_as use actual From/Into and map entities; callers must select the correct checked conversion. Diff serialization prefix reads native cursor/history and chooses snapshot or diffs; function tail291+ is unread. No global reflection/custom serde/native sender admission or component MapEntities proof from these generic SDK bodies."
